WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.837
Variables created inside a function usually belong to that function’s local workspace.

00:00:05.837 --> 00:00:10.172
That means outside code does not automatically see them.

00:00:10.172 --> 00:00:17.415
This is helpful because the internal details of one function do not have to interfere with the rest of the program.

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:24.612
When a useful result needs to leave the function, return provides a clean and explicit path.

00:00:24.612 --> 00:00:32.976
Think of the function as a small workspace: inputs enter, local work happens, and selected outputs are returned.
